// @@@ For all indices i in the list, if the new index is less than i but greater than or equal to the old index, the element at the new index is null and the element at the old index is also null, or they are equal. This implies that all elements before the new index are the same as before the old index.

--------------------
// @@@ For every index 'i' such that 'index' is less than 'i' and 'i' is less than the size of the list, the element at index 'i' should be null if it was null in the old state, or equal to the old state if it was not null. This implies that the element at index 'index' is being replaced with a null value.

--------------------
// @@@ For every index i from the specified index to the end of the list, the element at the new position is either null or equals to the old element at the same position. This implies that all the elements before the specified index remain the same after the set operation.

